    <string name="tour_welcome_title">Hello.\nLet me show you *your Home*.</string>
    <plurals name="tour_welcome_body">
        <item quantity="one">Just one stop, under a minute. Each card answers a question about your field.</item>
        <item quantity="other">%1$d stops, under a minute. Each card answers a question about your field.</item>
    </plurals>
    <string name="tour_today_title">Every morning I tell you *what to do today*.</string>
    <string name="tour_today_body">I read your phase, your weather and your plan, and sum it up in one sentence. Below is your week: the dot marks a day with a task.</string>
    <string name="tour_phase_title">Your phase, *as a countdown*.</string>
    <string name="tour_phase_body">How many days you have left to act and what comes next. Swipe the card to see the next phase of the olive.</string>
    <string name="tour_field_title">Your field, *at a glance*.</string>
    <string name="tour_field_body">Today\'s weather, your active alerts and the soil moisture your sensors measure. Tap any of them for the detail.</string>
    <string name="tour_alternation_title">Your alternation, *season by season*.</string>
    <string name="tour_alternation_body">Green is an ON year and yellow an OFF year. The dotted bar is my projection: if you thin on time, I soften next year\'s drop.</string>
    <string name="tour_plots_title">Every plot, *with its status*.</string>
    <string name="tour_plots_body">The label tells you if a plot needs attention, such as a critical load. Tap a plot to see its alternation, its plan or to edit it.</string>
    <string name="tour_register_title">Everything starts *down here*.</string>
    <string name="tour_register_body">Home, Plots, Plan and Logbook. With the + button you record a sampling, a thinning or a harvest in the field, even without signal.</string>
    <string name="tour_done_title">Ready. I\'ll let you know\n*about the rest*.</string>
    <string name="tour_done_body">If you want to go over it again, it is in My account › Home tour.</string>
